# Emberhollow, the village, on the longest night of the year.
# Where things stand: x to the right, z towards you (metres); you come in
# at the south edge, looking north (facing 0).

place the village
  title: Emberhollow
  the sky: night
  the mist: light
  the ground: moss, 46 by 46 m
  you come in at 0 13, facing 0

  a great hearth called the cold hearth at 0 -2, unlit
  Mira at -2.6 0.6, facing 30
  Tobin at 7.4 4.2, facing -70
  a well at 6 2.4

  a house called Mira's house at -9 -9, turned 35
  a house at 9.5 -8.5, turned -30
  a house at -12 4, turned 85
  a house at 12.5 5.5, turned -95
  a house at -4 -14, turned 5
  2 barrels in a line from -6.2 -6.6 to -5.5 -7.2
  a bench at 3.6 1.2, turned -90

  4 lamp posts in a line from -6 -5.5 to 6 -5.5, unlit
  2 lamp posts in a line from -2.2 8 to 2.2 8, unlit
  14 path stones in a line from 0 12 to 0 -15
  9 path stones in a line from -1.5 -1 to -15 -1

  a way to the woods at 0 -17
  a way to the hill at -17 -1, turned 90

  22 pine trees around 0 0, 19 to 23 m away
  8 tall pines around 0 0, 21 to 24 m away
  7 rocks between -16 -16 and 16 16

  when you first arrive
    say: The longest night of the year. Every lamp in Emberhollow went out at once, and the Hearthflame on the hill went out with them.
    say: Grey mist is already creeping between the houses. Old Mira, the lamplighter, is waiting by the cold hearth.

  when you talk to Mira
    if not met mira
      remember met mira
      Mira: There you are. Look at it. Sixty winters I have tended these lamps, and I have never seen them all go dark.
      Mira: It's the Hearthflame. When it dies, every fire it ever lit dies with it. And the Grey comes in behind.
      choose
        choice: What can we do?
          Mira: The old songs say the Hearthflame was born from three embers: one from the woods, one from the river, one from the peak.
        choice: Is it my fault? I was supposed to carry wood up the hill last night.
          Mira: Every family was supposed to carry wood up the hill. For years now, nobody has. If it's anyone's fault, it's all of ours.
          add 1 to kindness
      Mira: Bring the three embers to the Hearth on the hill, and the flame may wake again.
      Mira: Take my lantern. The spark inside is the last fire left in Emberhollow. Guard it.
      you get the old lantern
      say: You take the lantern. Its small light pushes the mist back a step.
      choose
        choice: I'll bring the fire back. I promise.
          add 1 to courage
          Mira: I know you will. The woods are north, past the last pines.
        choice: Why me? I'm only your apprentice.
          Mira: Because you're the one who still sings the old songs. Go north, into the woods.
    otherwise if embers is 3
      Mira: All three! I can feel the warmth from here. Go up the hill, before the Grey swallows the square.
    otherwise if embers is at least 1
      Mira: You found one! Can you feel how the mist pulls back from it?
      choose
        choice: Should I take it to the hill now?
          Mira: A small fire is better than none. But three embers would make a flame to last a hundred years. It's your choice.
        choice: I'll keep looking.
          Mira: Then go carefully. The river is past the woods, and the peak is up the river.
    otherwise
      Mira: North, into the woods. And keep that spark dry.

  when you talk to Tobin
    if tobin is brave
      Tobin: When the fire comes back, can I carry the first stick up the hill?
    otherwise
      Tobin: I'm not scared. I'm just standing very close to the well. In case the dark falls in.
      choose
        choice if you have the old lantern: It's all right to be scared. Here, hold the lantern a moment.
          say: Tobin wraps both hands around the lantern. Slowly his shoulders come down from his ears.
          Tobin: It's warm. Like Mum's oven. Oh! Mum baked this for whoever climbs the hill. I think that's you.
          you get the honey bread
          add 1 to kindness
          remember tobin is brave
        choice: It's all right to be scared. I am too.
          Tobin: You are? But you're nearly grown up.
          say: He thinks about it for a long time.
          Tobin: Mum baked bread for whoever climbs the hill. If you're scared too, you should have it. Being scared makes you hungry.
          you get the honey bread
          add 1 to kindness
          remember tobin is brave
        choice: Go home, Tobin. This is no night for children.
          Tobin: You're not much older than me.
          say: He doesn't move. Neither does the mist.

  when you look at the well
    say: Your light shivers on black water, far below. For a moment you think you see a second light down there, looking back up at you.

  when you look at the cold hearth
    if embers is 0
      say: The village hearth. Every evening its coals were lit from the Hearthflame on the hill. Tonight it's cold stone and ash.
    otherwise
      say: The ember you carry makes the ashes stir, as if they remember being fire.

  when you look at Mira's house
    say: Mira's house. Through the window you can see her candles, every one burned down to a stub.

  when you leave for the woods
    if you have the old lantern
      go to the woods
    otherwise
      say: The mist beyond the pines is as thick as wool. You won't get ten steps without a light. Mira is waiting by the hearth.

  when you leave for the hill
    if embers is 0
      say: The hill path climbs straight into the Grey. Without an ember there is nothing to give the Hearth.
    otherwise
      go to the hill
